Short: ReAction unarchive GUI for xfd/xadmaster
Uploader: chris@unsatisfactorysoftware.co.uk (Chris Young)
Author: chris@unsatisfactorysoftware.co.uk (Chris Young)
Type: util/arc
Version: 4.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.1; ppc-amigaos >= 4.1.0
Requires: util/arc/xadmaster000.lha

This is a simple GUI for xadmaster.library using the ReAction
gadget set, written as all the others on Aminet appear to
require MUI. It also supports decrunching with xfdmaster.library,
extracting various data with Deark, scanning for viruses with
xvs.library, and simple editing of LhA/Zip archives.

This is designed for AmigaOS 3.2.1+ (and tested on that and OS4). It
probably won't work on older versions as it needs a new window.class :)
All use is at your own risk.

GPL, source code available on website.

No AI generated code has been used in this application.
AI has occasionally been used to aid debugging.

Changes in this version:
* More modern looking GUI
  - All gadgets have been moved to a new toolbar
  - Built-in list and toolbar images have been redesigned and colourised
  - Extract (the most used button) is highlighted on the left!
  - Tabs have been added
  - Progress bar behaviour has been improved
  - Better feedback and status text
  - Button to select all on page
* Improved listview
  - Added extra fields (crunched size, comment, attributes)
  - Added checkboxes for directory items in browser mode
    NB: As AmigaOS does not have a "partially selected" checkbox state,
        a directory with some items selected will show as unchecked
  - Added icons for encrypted files, links and disk images
  - Amiga disk images (DMS) will now show as ADF if filesystem ignored
* Extract button now prompts for destination
  - New config to disable prompt and extract to a default location
* Added a "Create LhA archive" option to WB Tools menu
  - Quick way to create a new archive with the selected items
* Editing Zip archives now possible on OS3.2
  - Using Zip 2.32 comand-line tool
  - REGRESSION: Zip modifications are currently disabled on OS4
* Archive handling improvements
  - Can now open split archives (via Project=>Open=>Split archive...)
  - Can now open ADFs and other uncompressed disk formats
    (subject to the availability of a XAD filesystem module)
    NB: Ignore Filesystems applies here too, so disable if needed
  - Files with "encrypted info" should now open (untested)
  - Multiple files can now be selected to be opened in the ASL requester
* ARexx can now open in a new tab too


Note that due to a bug in v2.5 the "download updated version"
option is unlikely to work.  This was fixed in v3.1.

For full history see documentation inside the archive.
